Chief: ...Mayor -- I was

Mayor: What are you doing to save my goddamn city?

Chief: Your Honor, the army is on standby, we just need to fill in some forms...
Harlow: The army's no good here - it takes a trained professional to fully comprehend the intricacies of the baboon mind. You were right to call in the Federal Monkey Patrol - it's my call and I want first shot taking out those hairy bastards.

Mayor: You sound like a man of action! Is this one of your men, Chief?

Harlow: I'm Harlow, head of the Federal Monkey Patrol. The only way to deal with the simian threat is to take immediate action.

Mayor: You sound like you know what you're doing, I'm giving you emergency powers to use as you see fit. The resources of the city are at your disposal.

Chief: Please ignore this imbecile, Mayor. When the bureacrats made him top monkey man they never envisaged this. Harlow fill in the forms!

Harlow: Say Chief, your arms are rather hairy. Perhaps you have monkey sympathies?

Harlow: In extreme times like this a background check for known monkeys among your friends and family is not out of the question to assure your loyalty.

Chief: Harlow you idiot, everyone knows that apes and humans have a common ancestor, but this is stupid and beside the point

Harlow: Are you listening to this monkey-lover Mayor? He said you are no different from these monsters!

Mayor: God made monkey, then made man. How can they be related when they weren't even made on the same day? It's preposterous! Perhaps a background check is in order...

Chief: No. No. Ok Harlow you can be involved. There's a giant ape on 4th street that needs to be eliminated. We have firetrucks, safety nets, tranquiliser darts, ambulances all on standby. You can assist with...

Harlow: Never mind that stuff - it'll only slow me down. First, I'm gonna need a plane with two sets of wings, and enough lead to bring down a forty food gorilla.

Mayor: Get the man his plane!
